From: Keith Carter <oss@keithbcarter.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Stall watchdog, per-open retry of the source, give up on repeated failure

A stream that stops delivering frames (no frame for 3 s, e.g. a GPU hang mid-call)
now counts as a failure like a pipeline error. A failure restarts the pipeline,
on the fallback source if the main one failed. Every fresh start (new reader,
resume) tries the main source again, so a transient failure does not pin the
fallback until the service restarts. After 4 failures within 60 s the relay
stops retrying until the next open.
---
